\section{Head Coach \& Assistant Coaches Role Implementation}
\label{sec:impl-coaches}

Coaching staff own training and tactical decisions. The Head Coach has
full edit rights, Assistant Coaches have curated edit rights on
training plans and Goalkeeper Coaches are scoped to GK-position
players.

\subsection*{Coach Dashboard}

\textbf{Description:} Coach-centric pulse view: today's sessions,
players currently in rehab (read-only feed from the medical service),
next fixture, and outstanding training assessments.

\textbf{Key Features:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Today's sessions strip pulled from
        \texttt{training-match-service / sessions}.
  \item Rehab read-only sidebar pulled from
        \texttt{medical-fitness-service / injuries?status=ACTIVE}.
  \item Quick-create training session and quick-attach drill
        buttons.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Result:} The coach starts every day with a single screen
covering attendance, fitness and tactical state.

\screenshot{screenshots/coach-dashboard.png}%
{Coach Dashboard with today's sessions and the rehab read-only
 sidebar.}{fig:ss-coach-dashboard}

\subsection*{Training Page}

\textbf{Description:} Full lifecycle of training sessions: plans,
sessions, drills, attendance and per-player assessments.

\textbf{Key Features:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Create training plan with weekly cadence.
  \item Attach drills from the drill library (4 demo drills seeded).
  \item Record attendance per session per player.
  \item Write per-player assessments with rating and free-text
        observations.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Result:} Every demo session, plan, drill, attendance row and
assessment is consistent with the seeded match calendar, demonstrating
the end-to-end coaching loop.

\screenshot{screenshots/training.png}%
{Training page: plans, sessions, drills, attendance and assessments
 in a single view.}{fig:ss-training}

\subsection*{Formations \& Line-ups}

\textbf{Description:} Tactical authoring tool stored in
\texttt{training-match-service} as a \texttt{formation} entity with
attached \texttt{lineup} rows referencing players by
\texttt{playerId}.

\textbf{Key Features:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Drag-and-drop player slots on a tactical board.
  \item Position-aware constraints (a goalkeeper slot only accepts a
        GK-position player).
  \item Save as draft / publish for the upcoming match.
  \item Versioned formations reusable across matches.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Result:} The 1 formation + 4 line-ups in the demo seed map
cleanly onto the displayed tactical board.

\screenshot{screenshots/formations.png}%
{Formations \& Line-ups editor with the tactical board.}%
{fig:ss-formations}

\subsection*{Match Events Log}

\textbf{Description:} In-game event recorder for goals, cards,
substitutions and other key actions. Backed by the
\texttt{match\_events} table with a \texttt{minute} and
\texttt{event\_type} per row.

\textbf{Key Features:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Live-mode minute-by-minute entry.
  \item Event-type chips (GOAL, YELLOW, RED, SUB\_IN, SUB\_OUT).
  \item Per-event player attribution.
  \item Auto-rollup into the match's final stat-line.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Result:} The 4 demo events drive the visible match recap and
the per-player stats panel.

