\section{Medical Staff Role Implementation}
\label{sec:impl-medical}

Medical staff own everything in \texttt{mscms\_medical}: injuries,
diagnoses, treatments, rehabilitations, recovery programs, fitness
tests and training loads.

\subsection*{Medical Dashboard}

\textbf{Description:} A condensed view of the medical inbox tuned to
the staff member's specialty.

\textbf{Key Features:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Active injuries count grouped by severity.
  \item Players currently in rehab.
  \item Fitness tests scheduled for the next 14 days.
  \item Training-load alerts for players whose load exceeds the
        configured chronic-load ratio.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Result:} A medical staff member sees the day's priorities
at a glance.

\screenshot{screenshots/medical-dashboard.png}%
{Medical dashboard with active injuries grouped by severity.}%
{fig:ss-medical-dashboard}

\subsection*{Injuries Page}

\textbf{Description:} CRUD over the \texttt{injuries} table with
linked diagnoses, treatments and rehabilitation programs.

\textbf{Key Features:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Open new injury with player picker, injured-area chip and
        severity badge.
  \item Attach diagnosis records authored by the doctor.
  \item Attach treatment records authored by the physio.
  \item Attach rehab program authored by the fitness coach.
  \item Status pipeline: \texttt{ACTIVE}, \texttt{IN\_REHAB},
        \texttt{RECOVERED}.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Result:} The 2 demo injuries map to 2 diagnoses, 2
treatments, 2 rehabs and 2 recovery programs, demonstrating the full
cross-document chain.

\screenshot{screenshots/injuries.png}%
{Injuries page with the diagnosis / treatment / rehab side panel.}%
{fig:ss-injuries}

\subsection*{Fitness Tests \& Training Load}

\textbf{Description:} Fitness Coaches author \texttt{fitness\_tests}
rows (5 demo entries) and \texttt{training\_loads} rows (5 demo
entries) per player per session.

\textbf{Key Features:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Test-result entry with metric per discipline
        (VO\textsubscript{2} max for endurance, vertical jump for
        power).
  \item Training-load trend chart per player.
  \item Cross-reference against coach-authored training sessions.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Result:} A complete fitness/load history that informs both
the coaching staff (load management) and the medical staff
(injury-risk profiling).

\screenshot{screenshots/fitness-load.png}%
{Fitness tests and training-load trend chart per player.}%
{fig:ss-fitness}

