\section{Scout Role Implementation}
\label{sec:impl-scout}

The Scout role discovers and evaluates external talent.

\subsection*{Scout Dashboard}

\textbf{Description:} Pipeline view of in-progress scouting work.

\textbf{Key Features:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Reports in draft.
  \item Reports submitted and awaiting sport-manager decision.
  \item Recently approved transfers originating from this scout.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Result:} A scout sees the conversion rate of their own
pipeline.

\subsection*{Outer Players Page}

\textbf{Description:} Catalogue of external players (rival teams and
free agents) modelled in \texttt{player-management-service}. 4 demo
outer players are seeded (Real Madrid CF, Atl\'etico, Sevilla, RM
Baloncesto representatives).

\textbf{Key Features:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Filter by team, position, age range.
  \item Per-player profile with cross-references to existing scout
        reports.
  \item Quick \texttt{Create scout report} action.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Result:} A single catalogue of every prospect the club is
watching, with workflow continuity to the scout-report tool.

\screenshot{screenshots/outer-players.png}%
{Outer Players catalogue with rival-team filtering.}%
{fig:ss-outer-players}

\subsection*{Scout Reports Page}

\textbf{Description:} CRUD over \texttt{scout\_reports} rows with
structured ratings (technical, physical, tactical, mental, potential)
and free-text observations.

\textbf{Key Features:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Five-axis radar chart for technical / physical / tactical /
        mental / potential scores.
  \item Recommendation chip (\texttt{SIGN}, \texttt{MONITOR},
        \texttt{REJECT}).
  \item Forwards selected reports to the sport manager.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Result:} The 4 demo scout reports drive the incoming-transfer
queue visible to the sport manager.

\screenshot{screenshots/scout-reports.png}%
{Scout Reports page with the five-axis radar chart.}%
{fig:ss-scout-reports}

